{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"eb1c625da8127398680f43df043f688be2be1a07ab9d99a86b8b18f1d068db6a","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate drift-refresh mechanism","key_entities":["progressive_drift_refresh","src/rebar/_config_schema.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","docs/config.md","docs/plan-review-gate.md","docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md","E4","G1G2","AGENT_TIER"],"problem_keywords":["plan review attestation","stale verdict","code drift","re-review instability","full criteria re-sampling","progressive drift-refresh","grounding probe","configuration default"],"propositions":["When main advances, signed plan-review attestations become stale and trigger re-review of byte-identical plans, causing full criteria re-sampling with 32% verdict instability despite unchanged material fingerprint.","Progressive drift-refresh probe (scoped E4+G1G2 grounding) exists and can refresh stale attestations without full re-review, but ships disabled pending latency/token measurement never taken.","Progressive drift-refresh must be flipped from default False to True in VerifyConfig, with explicit False restoring full re-review fallback for back-out.","A drift-only-stale re-review under default config must take the scoped probe path (2 agent-tier criteria) instead of full criteria set (~12 agent-tier criteria), reducing LLM work by ~75-83%.","All default-OFF framing about drift-refresh across src/, tests/, and docs/ must be replaced with default-ON framing, with dated operator authorization and explicit False as the back-out mechanism."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785822345780358988,"uuid":"525d8768-c2af-4ead-89a1-8b4e93dee07a"}